:"MCTM-029894","value":"1.55 ± 0.11","numeric":1.55}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-029895","Abbreviation_in_the_article":3,"Cell_line":"K-562","Time(h)":72,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"15.2 ± 4.08","IC50_Dark_value":15.2,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1039/b902748c","Year":2009,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-029895","value":"18.0 ± 2.62","numeric":18}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":3,"value":-1.45,"value_relation":"=","std":0.08,"type_authors":"logD","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"PBS","pH":7.4,"doi":"10.1039/b902748c","year":2009,"record_id":"MLDB-001026","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The octanol–water partition coefficients of the compounds 1–5were determined using a shake-flask method. PBS buffered doubly distilled water (100 mL, phosphate buffer, c(PO43-) = 10 mM,c(NaCl) = 0.15 M, pH adjusted to 7.4 and 6.8 with HCl) and n- octanol (100 mL) were shaken together using a laboratory shaker (Perkin-Elmer), for 72 h to allow saturation of both the phases. 1 mg of each compound was mixed in 1 mL of aqueous and organic phase, respectively for 10 min using a laboratory vortexer. The resultant emulsion was centrifuged (3000 ¥ g, 5 min) to separate the phases. The concentrations of the complex in the organic and aqueous phases were then determined using UV absorbance spectroscopy (260 nm). LogDpH was defined as the logarithm of the ratio of the concentrations of the complex in the organic and aqueous phases (logD = log{[Au(org)]/[Au(aq)]}; the value reported is the mean of three separate determinations."}]}